    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443-a3">

                <pb facs="0792" n="696" xml:id="pg696"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 108.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Harry Parkes to Mr. Bingham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Yedo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1874-08-04"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 4,
                    1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Having been informed by the agent of the
                    Oriental Bank at Yokohama that he has received from the vice-minister for
                    foreign affairs, on my account, another installment of the Simonoseki indemnity,
                    amounting to $125,000, I have the honor to inform you that, for the reasons
                    stated in my dispatch to you of the 23d February last, I have instructed the
                    manager of the Oriental Bank to pay over to you the sum of $5,833.33.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HARRY S. PARKES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
